_delta","text":" collisions?**\n\nTwo"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" different keys can"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" produ"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ce the same bucket number"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"."},{"type":"text_delta","text":" This is called"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" a **collision**. Common"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" fixes:"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n- **Chaining:**"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" each"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" bucket holds a small"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" list of"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" p"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"airs. You"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" check the list in"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" that bucket for"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" the mat"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ching key.\n- **Open"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" addressing:** if"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" a"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" bucket is ta"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ken, try"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" the next emp"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ty one."},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nGood hash ma"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ps ke"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ep coll"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"isions rare by growing the"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" number"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" of buckets when"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" they"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" start"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" to"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" fill up."},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n**Why it's use"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ful**\n\n- Coun"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ting things"},{"type":"text_delta","text":": `coun"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ts[\"ap"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ple\"] += 1`"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n- Ca"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ching results"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" you"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"'ve"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" already computed\n- Looking"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" up users"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" by "},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ID, or sett"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ings by name\n\n**Qu"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ick summary:"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"** A hash map"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" run"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"s the"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" key through a function to"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" get a location"},{"type":"text_delta","text":", so it"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" can store"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" and retrieve values directly"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" inst"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ead of sear"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ching through them"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" one"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" by one."},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"A **hash map** (also called a dictionary or hash table) stores pairs of **keys** and **values**, and it can find a value from its key very quickly.\n\n**The basic idea**\n\nImagine a row of 10 numbered mailboxes. You want to store a phone number for \"Alice.\" Instead of checking every mailbox, you use a formula that turns the name into a mailbox number:\n\n```\n\"Alice\" → hash function → 3\n```\n\nThe **hash function** takes the key and produces a number (the \"bucket\" or index). You put Alice's phone number in bucket 3. Later, when you want Alice's number, you run the same function on \"Alice,\" get 3, and look there. You don't search everything.\n\n**Step by step**\n\n1. **Store:** `map[\"Alice\"] = \"555-1234\"`\n   - Hash \"Alice\" → index 3\n   - Put `(\"Alice\", \"555-1234\")` in bucket 3.\n2. **Look up:** `map[\"Alice\"]`\n   - Hash \"Alice\" → index 3\n   - Go straight to bucket 3 and return the value.\n\nBecause you jump directly to the right spot, lookups are usually very fast, roughly constant time, no matter how many items are stored.\n\n**What about collisions?**\n\nTwo different keys can produce the same bucket number. This is called a **collision**. Common fixes:\n\n- **Chaining:** each bucket holds a small list of pairs. You check the list in that bucket for the matching key.\n- **Open addressing:** if a bucket is taken, try the next empty one.\n\nGood hash maps keep collisions rare by growing the number of buckets when they start to fill up.\n\n**Why it's useful**\n\n- Counting things: `counts[\"apple\"] += 1`\n- Caching results you've already computed\n- Looking up users by ID, or settings by name\n\n**Quick summary:** A hash map runs the key through a function to get a location, so it can store and retrieve values directly instead of searching through them one by one."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":655,"cache_read_input_tokens":4517,"cache_creation_input_tokens":89},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
